          "A claims desk loses track of multiple loss contact log when the rule exists only in a shift note, so Virtual Claims Assistant puts it in the multi-loss contact log. The item opens at a policyholder reports a second loss under the same policy and closes only after file, split, or escalate the contact is dated and signed by a reviewer. The contact log assistant gathers the policy and loss references and the contact date and channel; the claims supervisor keeps the call that changes coverage, payment, or a policyholder promise. A later examiner should be able to rebuild the sequence from the file without a phone call.",
          "No one can keep multiple loss contact log in memory when claim volume doubles overnight. The multi-loss contact log carries the claim reference, the owner, and the next action so coverage does not depend on recall. The contact log assistant prepares the file and the claims supervisor makes the determination that binds the carrier. Each item has a diary date, which is what makes the control real."
