          "The total loss rental review file at Virtual Claims Assistant keeps the examiner observation apart from the coverage conclusion. It carries the policy number, the document version, the reviewer, and pay, adjust, or close the rental. When two records conflict, keep both and send the narrow question to the claims supervisor. That practice holds up during a reinspection, an appraisal, or a policyholder dispute."
